<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Azerbaijan SSR</h1><p class="st-meta">1920 CE – 1991 CE · capital Baku</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Soviet Azerbaijan, a republic of the USSR from 1920 to 1991, centred on oil-rich Baku and shaped by the conflict over Nagorno-Karabakh.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In April 1920 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baku">Baku</a>, and the Bolsheviks overthrew the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan-democratic-republic">Azerbaijan Democratic Republic</a>, proclaiming the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> Soviet Socialist Republic. In 1922 it joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/transcaucasian-sfsr">Transcaucasian SFSR</a>, which became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, and in 1936 it became a full union republic.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baku">Baku's</a> oil fields were vital to the Soviet economy, especially in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. The republic included the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagorno-karabakh-autonomous-oblast">Nagorno-Karabakh Autonomous Oblast</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nakhchivan-autonomous-soviet-socialist-republic">Nakhchivan ASSR</a>. Soviet rule brought industrialisation, mass literacy and a switch from Arabic to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> and then Cyrillic script, but also collectivisation and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-stalin">Stalin</a>'s purges. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heydar-aliyev">Heydar Aliyev</a> led the republic's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-the-soviet-union">Communist Party</a> from 1969 to 1982.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>From 1988 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karabakh-movement">Karabakh movement</a> led to war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenians">Armenians</a>, and Soviet troops killed over a hundred civilians in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baku">Baku</a> in January 1990. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> declared independence in August 1991, and the USSR's dissolution in December 1991 created the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/azerbaijan-ssr.jpg" alt="Azerbaijan SSR" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Azerbaijan_Soviet_Socialist_Republic_(1952%E2%80%931991).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1920 CE – 1991 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Baku</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Heydar Aliyev, Ayaz Mutallibov</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Shia Islam (officially atheist state)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Azerbaijani; Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Azerbaijan Soviet Socialist Republic, Soviet Azerbaijan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1956&amp;focus=azerbaijan-ssr" aria-label="Azerbaijan SSR on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5904 735 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Azerbaijan SSR lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6224 991L6224 991M6224 991L6090 947M6224 991L5820 533M6224 991L6224 991"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6224 991h0M6090 947h0M5820 533h0M6224 991h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6224 991h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6224 991h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Baku. <a href="/atlas?year=1956&amp;focus=azerbaijan-ssr">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
